From f5f975478fa2dd4a45178f257338af65b6547dc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rationalsa <belaboxproject@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:02:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fm350gl: forward-port USB RNDIS bearer and mode handling

Description: Add the FM350-GL USB/RNDIS bearer and GTACT mode handling on 1.24.2
 This is a source-level re-implementation of BELABOX's FM350-GL plugin against
 ModemManager 1.24.2. It uses the current MMIfaceModemInterface and GTask APIs,
 activates/deactivates the RNDIS PDP context with +CGACT, obtains addressing
 through +CGPADDR/+CGCONTRDP, and returns the network port instead of attempting
 the generic PPP ATD path. The FM350-specific first-enable override sends ATZ0
 instead of the unsupported ATZ form. The 4-second GMR guard, IPv4-only DNS
 relaxation, set-mode completion fix, and single-RAT stale-preference fix are
 folded here.
 .
 The bearer parses the FM350's +CGCONTRDP answer itself, as BELABOX's plugin
 did: one line per IP family, an empty bearer id (which the generic parser
 rejects), IPv6 in dotted decimal, the MTU, and the older layout with a
 separate subnet field. A malformed line is skipped. An answer without a
 usable line is not fatal once +CGPADDR has given the address; an error
 answer, cancellation or timeout still fails the connection.
Author: rationalsa <belaboxproject@gmail.com>
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/BELABOX/modemmanager/commit/da01610c46c581b0c6f2acd0ac50f5bba666efdf
