Bug: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/ModemManager/-/issues/899
Forwarded: no (merge request drafted but not filed; no upstream MR URL exists)
Applied-Upstream: no
Upstream-Status: NOT UPSTREAM; no USB/RNDIS fm350gl plugin exists in 1.24.2 or upstream main
Rationale: The USB 0e8d:7126/7127 compositions expose RNDIS plus AT ports but no MBIM/QMI port. Generic ModemManager therefore issues ATD*99***N# and the modem returns 0,NONE. The bearer must use +CGACT and the RNDIS net port.
Credit: BELABOX-authored fixes forward-ported by CeraLive; this patch is not CeraLive-originated work. The +CGCONTRDP parser restores BELABOX's tolerance of the FM350 answer that the forward-port had lost.
Last-Update: 2026-11-23

